  "interpretation": [
    "The handshake is authenticated. The truncated application record never completes server AEAD verification or produces plaintext; the relay sees a full ciphertext record from the client and deliberately drops its tail.",
    "Initial actual READ raw0/WANT_READ2 creates a retry and partial buffer; two immutable refused samples. Same original buffer, length and sentinel are verified before and after the EOF retry.",
    "The relay pauses backend reads to keep the native fatal alert from triggering a client error/RST race. It ends only its server-facing TCP leg; the client stays owned and alive. No blanket error suppression.",
    "One original READ retry must report raw0/SSL_ERROR_SSL1/firstSSLqueue reason294/amount0. RST/clean close/success/retry is not a substitute.",
    "Fatal return is followed only by immutable refused metadata and cleanup; no TLS read/write/control/handshake/shutdown call. Retained READ retry is old coarse ledger bookkeeping, not permission to execute it again.",
    "Observed initial1172 and fatal2196 are scoped reason masks. Existing WRITE_CALL1024 is based on rwstate!=SSL_NOTHING and can appear on READ/WANT_READ; it does not establish an outstanding WRITE. Generic probe/ledger semantics are unchanged.",
    "Fatal handling inside the READ may emit an alert and advance output sequence. Metadata sequence observations are not independently wire-validated here.",
    "wire=null, graceful=false; no full captured-stream oracle, serverFIN, graceful closure or direct-client-truncation claim. Two TCP legs and an explicit relay fault injector are not migration.",
    "Only one default Node ciphertext record, payload<=16384 and a strictly internal body prefix are supported by this new case. Other header/RST/truncation variants stay separate; no global cap increase.",
    "Baseline rejects unsupported scenario before build/TLS; new coverage is not an OpenSSL production bug claim. Option controls are no-TLS checks separate from the canonical21 and heldouts.",
    "Native499 source files, LICENSE, alpha guards and prior20 test bytes are preserved. Historical alpha failure/cause uncertainty and all adverse/setup results remain recorded."
  ],
